# Python style

Ruff and mypy (strict) already enforce formatting, types, imports, `print`, and mutable
defaults. Beyond that:

- Validate data crossing an external boundary (API, LLM output, file, env) on entry.
  Pydantic for external contracts, dataclasses for small internal value objects.
  No model without a clear boundary.
- Raise specific domain errors, defined in one module. Never swallow an error silently.
- No module-level side effects or global mutable state. Config only through `Settings`.
- Keep functions focused. Do not split or combine them to satisfy a line count.
  Prefer pure functions; isolate I/O.
- No docstrings. Add a one-line comment only for a constraint the code cannot show.
